# OWNER-LOGIN DEPLOYMENT — the SHARED DATABASE env file. ONE login (crewflow_owner) for the API (which migrates on start,
# O3) and the Worker. Template only: copy to ${CREWFLOW_SECRETS_DIR}/database.env (root:root 0600) and fill every
# <placeholder> from the secret store. docker-compose.image.yml reads this ONE file on rab-api and rab-worker, so
# PG_DATABASE_URL is byte-identical on both. Staging uses the same template with staging-only values.
# Lint the real file before every release (prints names and reasons only, never values):
#   node packages/rab-docker/scripts/compose-owner-login.cjs --lint-env-file database ${CREWFLOW_SECRETS_DIR}/database.env
#
# DATABASE. crewflow_owner, created by the provider admin with the one-time SQL (OWNER-LOGIN-DEPLOYMENT.md section 4:
# postgres-init/owner-login/01-crewflow-owner.sql for a fresh database, transition-from-separated.sql for an existing
# separated one), at the provider's DIRECT host (never a transaction pooler: Neon -pooler, Supabase :6543, DigitalOcean
# :25061, RDS Proxy, PgBouncer :6432), TLS verify-full. NEVER the provider's default admin login (neondb_owner, doadmin,
# the RDS master, Supabase postgres, Cloud SQL postgres, the Azure admin) and never a former separated login (crewflow_app,
# crewflow, crewflow_worker, crewflow_migrator): those are schema roles now, not runtime logins.
# Bundled database (docker-compose.local-db.yml): host rab-postgres, database crewflow.
PG_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://crewflow_owner:<crewflow_owner-password>@<db-direct-host>:5432/<db-name>?sslmode=verify-full
# The CA that signed the server certificate; the compose file mounts CREWFLOW_PG_CA_FILE here. Do not change the path.
PG_SSL_CA_CERT_PATH=/run/crewflow/pg-ca.crt
PG_EXPECTED_DATABASE_NAME=<db-name>
#
# DEPLOYMENT IDENTITY: OPTIONAL (BC-11, owner decision 2026-11-05). When declared, every process (and the API's migration
# child) matches it against the database's identity marker and refuses a mismatch; when absent, they warn and continue. The id is
# a UUID generated once per deployment (uuidgen) and kept; never reuse another deployment's id (staging has its own).
# CREWFLOW_DEPLOYMENT_ENVIRONMENT=production
# CREWFLOW_DEPLOYMENT_ID=<deployment-uuid>
#
# APPROVAL MODE: NOT here (O3). It is an interpolation value of compose.env (none by default, token an opt-in, BC-11/C4);
# rab-api's committed ${CREWFLOW_MIGRATION_APPROVAL_MODE:-none} would silently override a value here, so the lint refuses it.
#
# MUST NOT BE SET in this file (the lint refuses each; the runtime env validation refuses most, with an actionable message):
#   - any second database URL: DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED, DATABASE_DIRECT_URL, PG_WORKER_DATABASE_URL,
#     CREWFLOW_PROVISIONER_DATABASE_URL, CREWFLOW_MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL, CREWFLOW_PRESTART_MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL,
#     PG_DATABASE_REPLICA_URL (and the PG_DATABASE_REPLICA_* tuning), PG_OPS_APP_DATABASE_URL, POSTURE_DATABASE_URL,
#     DRIFT_DATABASE_URL, TEST_DATABASE_*. There is exactly one URL;
#   - CREWFLOW_MIGRATION_APPROVED (with token mode, passed to the one API start only, never in a file) and
#     CREWFLOW_UPGRADE_INCOMPLETE (api-prestart.sh
#     sets it itself after a failed upgrade; an inherited value is refused);
#   - role passwords and command authority: CREWFLOW_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD, CREWFLOW_APP_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD,
#     CREWFLOW_WORKER_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD, CREWFLOW_MIGRATOR_PASSWORD, CREWFLOW_MIGRATION_PHASE,
#     CREWFLOW_DEPLOYMENT_IDENTITY_BOOTSTRAP, ALLOW_PRODUCTION_DB_COMMANDS, DB_TARGET, DB_POOL_MAX, BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_*;
#   - CREWFLOW_DB_MODE (there is no mode switch; the owner login is the only architecture);
#   - the libpq variables (PGHOST, PGPORT, PGUSER, PGPASSWORD, PGDATABASE, PGSSLMODE, PGSERVICE, PGPASSFILE, ...);
#   - CREWFLOW_OPS_*, NODE_OPTIONS;
#   - anything committed in the compose files (NODE_ENV, RAB_RUNTIME_ENV, CREWFLOW_MIGRATE_ON_START,
#     DISABLE_DB_MIGRATIONS, DISABLE_CRON_JOBS_REGISTRATION, CREWFLOW_RUNTIME_ISOLATION, WORKER_FAST_PUBLISH_NOTIFY,
#     WORKER_EMAIL_DISPATCH_INTERVAL_SECONDS, WORKER_TIMER_TRIGGERS, WORKER_TIMER_TRIGGER_KINDS,
#     WORKER_OFFER_EXPIRY_INTERVAL_SECONDS, WORKER_MANAGER_CONFIRMATION_TIMEOUT_INTERVAL_SECONDS,
#     WORKER_LATE_CLOCK_IN_INTERVAL_SECONDS, WORKER_SHIFT_STATEMENT_DISPATCH_INTERVAL_SECONDS, ...);
#     CREWFLOW_MIGRATION_APPROVAL_MODE
#     (compose.env only);
#   - the deprecated CREWFLOW_UPGRADE_FAILURE_POLICY (use CREWFLOW_UPGRADE_FAILURE in runtime.env, or leave it unset);
#   - the runtime secrets of runtime.env (APP_SECRET, REDIS_URL, S3_*, EMAIL_*, ...).
